From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: the prefix arrives booted, so do not run wineboot.

With the user shared data mapped (0744, 0745), Wine reaches the end of its
process initialisation and stops at the one thing a title cannot do:

    trace:process:NtCreateUserProcess process creation is not supported on PS5
    err:environ:run_wineboot failed to start wineboot c00000bb

c00000bb is STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED. wineboot is a separate executable, and
NtCreateUserProcess has never been available here.

It also has nothing to do. The prefix is built by Wine on a host and copied to
the console whole -- registry, system32 and all -- so it arrives in the state
wineboot would leave it in. Signal the event the rest of the process waits on
and return.

Falling through instead would wait the full five minutes for a process that
cannot start, report a timeout, and carry on anyway.

virtual_init_user_shared_data still runs: it fills in the shared data the
process needs regardless of who booted the prefix.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -1582,6 +1582,22 @@ static void run_wineboot( WCHAR *env, SIZE_T size )
     }
 
     virtual_init_user_shared_data();
+
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ A title cannot create a process -- NtCreateUserProcess answers
+     * STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED -- so wineboot cannot run here:
+     *
+     *     trace:process:NtCreateUserProcess process creation is not supported
+     *     err:environ:run_wineboot failed to start wineboot c00000bb
+     *
+     * It has nothing to do either. The prefix is built by Wine on a host and
+     * copied to the console whole, registry and all, so it arrives booted.
+     * Signal the event the rest of the process waits on and carry on; falling
+     * through would wait five minutes for a process that cannot start. */
+    NtSetEvent( handles[0], NULL );
+    goto wait;
+#endif
+
     env[size] = 0;
     params.Flags           = PROCESS_PARAMS_FLAG_NORMALIZED;
     params.Environment     = env;
-- 
